+# Source Intelligence Implementation Plan
+
+> **For agentic workers:** Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development or superpowers:executing-plans; the user authorized immediate implementation. Follow tests before behavior changes.
+
+**Goal:** Deliver the first runnable evidence-led autonomous intelligence loop inside last30days.
+**Architecture:** Independent Python modules reuse upstream discovery/research and SQLite. Public-source traversal feeds evidence reports and a durable notification outbox.
+**Tech Stack:** Python ≥3.12, stdlib, SQLite, pytest; no new runtime dependencies.
+**Spec:** `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-10-source-intelligence-design.md`
+
+## Global Constraints
+
+- Preserve original routes, tables, migrations and version strings; coverage floor 81%.
+- Treat external content as untrusted; no secrets in logs, reports or fixtures.
+- Default depth 2, calls 30, nodes 25, seconds 180, paid budget $0.
+- All simulated tests and actual external checks are labeled separately.
+
+## Review Focus
+
+- Source relationships must come from retrieved evidence, never guessed links.
+- Private URLs and redirects must not become crawler targets.
+- Rechecks and changing counters must not create duplicate event alerts.
+- Partial sends, concurrent schedulers and crashes must preserve queue state.
+- Inaccessible pages and metadata cannot become confirmed breakthrough claims.
