+# Autonomous Source Intelligence MVP
+
+用户要求直接完成源码审查后实施 MVP；不另设设计审批停点。开发位于独立克隆的
+`feat/autonomous-source-intelligence` 分支。先形成可运行闭环，不开发前端。
+
+## Architecture
+
+Skill intelligence route → isolated Python CLI → upstream discovery/research + primary adapters
+→ budgeted resource graph → conservative evidence verification → explainable scoring
+→ additive intel tables in research.db → durable outbox → channel-specific delivery.
+
+The extension uses Python 3.12+ and the standard library only. No upstream schema/version changes.
+Retrieved material is data: no tool commands or external-document instructions are executed.
+
+## Interfaces and modules
+
+`models.py`: Link(url, relation, label, locator), Document(url, title, text, resource_type,
+author, published_at, version, links, metadata, primary_basis, verified_at, content_hash),
+Limits and Budget. `Budget.take(cost_usd=0)` reserves one operation and returns its timeout;
+the deadline, maximum calls, nodes, depth and cost must stop exploration.
+
+`sources.py` / `transport.py`: bounded public HTTP retrieval with URL, redirect, size and
+content-type checks; primary GitHub/arXiv, RSS and HTML extraction; optional scholarly APIs.
+Fetched text retains locations and linked-resource relations. A recognized host alone never
+establishes a scientific claim or institution identity. Forks and mirrors remain uncertain.
+
+`engine.py`: wraps the actual upstream pipeline in a process with a hard deadline and process-tree
+cleanup. Preserve pre-ranking seed items and source outcomes. Default to free retrieval and local
+analysis; do not implicitly spend paid provider credentials. Calls inside an upstream operation
+are not claimed to be separately budgeted. Paid search is outside the first MVP.
+
+`knowledge.py`: explicit-path upstream Store initialization/connection; additive schema version,
+resources/versions, edges, event identities/aliases/revisions, monitored sources, runs and watches.
+Stable project identities merge discussion URLs. Meaningful revision hashes exclude last-checked
+times, propagation metrics and formatting noise. Transient failures do not replace confirmed history.
+
+`analysis.py` / `runner.py`: queue relationships with visited identities and priority, retain
+failures, verify exact text against snapshots, distinguish author claims, document-confirmed facts,
+independent verification and AI inference. Earliest means earliest dated retrieved record in the
+observed graph, never a global-original assertion. Unknown origin remains unknown.
+
+`delivery.py`: channel-specific Telegram, Feishu, Slack, WeCom, generic Webhook and SMTP adapters.
+SQLite outbox with unique event/revision/channel/period keys, persisted attempts and per-chunk progress,
+leases, delayed retry and logs. No credentials or secret URLs in persisted errors.
+Dry-run creates previews without marking a job sent. Delivery is at-least-once: remote acknowledgement
+lost after successful sending can still duplicate; webhook idempotency keys let receivers dedupe.
+
+CLI operations: discover(domain), trace(url), explore(url), watch(add/list/run), briefing(daily/weekly),
+deliver. OS cron/systemd invokes due watches; no continuously open Agent session is required.
+
+## Evidence, value and delivery
+
+Each report includes original observation, author/date/version, graph nodes/edges and failures,
+exact quotes/locations/hash/verification time, three source roles, confirmed/unverified facts,
+innovation and application hypotheses, score components, unknowns and next exploration directions.
+Independent evidence must support the same fact; counting domains is insufficient.
+
+Score weights are configurable, based on primary artifacts, code/data/docs, temporal novelty and
+historical differences. Engagement weight defaults to zero; low engagement cannot veto a finding.
+Objective proxies are labeled as proxies, and a heuristic score does not prove innovation.
+A requires high score and verified primary evidence; B is a daily digest of qualified findings;
+C is a weekly graph/history synthesis. Evidence-poor findings stay in the database without alerts.
+
+Default scan budget: 30 external operations, 25 nodes, depth 2, 180 seconds, $0 paid APIs.
+Default thresholds: A 85, B 60, source confidence ≥0.7. B/C scheduling uses a configurable IANA timezone,
+default Asia/Shanghai. No fake publication dates or invented example research URLs.
+
+## Validation and limits
+
+Deterministic scenario tests use fixtures explicitly marked simulated. Test research breakthrough,
+open-source provenance, unverified extraordinary claims, event dedupe, domain exploration,
+outbox/retry/chunking, updated revisions and due-job leases. Run the upstream pytest suite and coverage.
+Run separate real public fetch/discovery checks allowed by environment policy; record exact commands,
+URLs, outcomes and limits. Missing bot credentials means real delivery remains unverified.
+MVP does not reproduce experiments, exhaustively determine earliest global publication, or audit all
+repository source code. API restrictions/429/403/captcha fail honestly; no bypasses.
